# Examples Consistency - drift discipline for examples/ and the sync skill

> Status: **Approved** - owner decisions incorporated. Implementation not
> started yet.
> Origin: nimbus (cloudflare/nimbus) review discussion - its "canonical source
> -> generator -> verified artifacts" model, scaled down to this repo's
> `examples/` + sync skill.

## Why

`examples/` ships four sample external repos (my-posts, vite-docs, astro-docs,
json-server-docs). Each carries a copy of the `site-content-sync` skill
(SKILL.md + validate.mjs + apply-delete-list.mjs + two workflow templates).
Today:

- The skill is hand-duplicated 4x. A hub-side contract change (adding a
  locale, changing a frontmatter rule, extending `sync-delete.list` syntax)
  requires editing the same files in four places, and nothing enforces that
  they stay identical.
- `validate.mjs` hardcodes `SUPPORTED_LOCALES = ['en', 'zh-Hans']` - exactly
  the kind of drift nimbus's generator model prevents.
- The examples are inconsistent in what they carry: my-posts and vite-docs
  include their `.github/workflows/` file, astro-docs and json-server-docs do
  not. astro-docs additionally demonstrates the `landing/` feature; the
  others do not.
- Nothing verifies that an example's content still passes its own validator,
  or that the example schemas still match the hub's `content.config.ts`.

Goal: one canonical skill copy + a generator to re-sync the other copies + a
CI check that fails on drift (nimbus's `templates-check` in miniature). This
is the "examples consistency CI" from the review discussion; the full
generator-from-manifest model is deferred (we are not generating repo variants
yet).

## Approach

### 1. Canonical skill home

New directory `examples/_shared/site-content-sync/` becomes the single source
of truth (SKILL.md + scripts/ + templates/). It is *not* itself a sample repo
- it is the canonical tree the examples copy from. (Alternative rejected:
using `examples/my-posts/...` as canonical ties the canonical copy to one
example's identity; `_shared` keeps it neutral, mirroring nimbus's
canonical-source tree.)

The skill's SKILL.md keeps its current generic wording (placeholders
`<HUB_REPO>` / `<HUB_TOKEN_SECRET>`), so it is repo-agnostic and copyable.

### 2. Generator: `scripts/sync-examples.mjs`

- Copies `examples/_shared/site-content-sync/**` into each example's
  `skills/site-content-sync/`, overwriting (nimbus: hand-edits happen in one
  place; the copies are sync output).
- Idempotent; prints what changed; exits 0.
- Also normalizes the presence of `.github/workflows/sync-*.yml` per example
  so all four examples carry the same workflow set (decision 2): astro-docs
  and json-server-docs get their `sync-docs.yml`; my-posts keeps
  `sync-posts.yml`; vite-docs keeps `sync-docs.yml`.

### 3. Drift guard: `scripts/check-examples.mjs`

- For each example: byte-compare `skills/site-content-sync/**` against the
  canonical tree; report diffs, exit non-zero.
- For each example: `cd` into it and run its own `validate.mjs` against its
  content (proves the validator works and the example content is valid).
- Optional cross-check: read the hub's `content.config.ts` schemas and flag
  when an example's documented frontmatter rules disagree. v1: skipped - too
  much parsing; the byte-compare + validator run already catches drift.

### 4. CI: `.github/workflows/examples-check.yml` (implemented but OFF)

- The workflow is written with the full path-filtered `pull_request` logic
  (`examples/**`, `skills/**`, `scripts/**`), but the PR trigger is disabled
  by default (owner decision 3): the file ships with `workflow_dispatch`
  active so it can be run manually, and the `pull_request` event block is
  present but commented out with an "enable by uncommenting" note. Manual
  builds stay manual.
- Runs `node scripts/check-examples.mjs` (via `npm run check:examples`).
- Does **not** run a full `npm ci` + `astro build` in this job (expensive);
  a heavier "sync-simulate then build" job can be added later as a
  `workflow_dispatch`.

### 5. Docs

- AGENTS.md: one paragraph - "hand-edit the skill only under
  `examples/_shared/site-content-sync/`; run `npm run sync:examples` to
  propagate; `npm run check:examples` gates drift."
- `examples/_shared/site-content-sync/SKILL.md` gains a header note that it
  is the canonical copy and generated copies must not be hand-edited.

## Files touched

| File | Change |
|---|---|
| `examples/_shared/site-content-sync/**` | **new** - canonical skill tree (moved from one example's current copy) |
| `examples/*/skills/site-content-sync/**` | regenerated from canonical (content identical today) |
| `scripts/sync-examples.mjs` | **new** - generator |
| `scripts/check-examples.mjs` | **new** - drift guard + per-example validate run |
| `.github/workflows/examples-check.yml` | **new** - path-filtered PR check; PR trigger disabled by default (manual `workflow_dispatch` only until enabled) |
| `package.json` | add `sync:examples` + `check:examples` scripts |
| `AGENTS.md` | canonical-copy rule paragraph |

## Decisions (resolved, owner review)

1. **Canonical location: `examples/_shared/site-content-sync/`.**
2. **Unify workflows: yes.** The generator normalizes each example's
   `.github/workflows/` so all four carry the same set.
3. **PR detection: implemented but not enabled.** The workflow ships with
   path-filtered `pull_request` logic ready but the trigger off
   (`workflow_dispatch` only until flipped on). Manual builds stay manual.
4. **Hub-side `.agents/skills/awareride-content-sync/` stays out of scope** -
   it is the AwareRide-specific real-world skill, not a template artifact.

## Implementation order

1. Move one example's skill tree to `examples/_shared/site-content-sync/`.
2. Write `scripts/sync-examples.mjs`; run it to (re)generate all copies,
   including the unified `.github/workflows/` set (decision 2).
3. Write `scripts/check-examples.mjs`; `npm run check:examples` passes.
4. Add the (disabled-by-default) workflow + package.json scripts +
   AGENTS.md note.

## Verification checklist

- `npm run check:examples` passes on a clean tree.
- Deliberately edit one example's SKILL.md -> `check:examples` fails with a
  clear diff (then restore).
- `npm run build` still passes (hub untouched).
- Each example's `validate.mjs` still passes against its own content.
- The workflow runs manually via `workflow_dispatch`; the PR trigger stays
  off until explicitly enabled.

## Out of scope

- Full generator-from-manifest (variants / `templates` branches) - deferred
  until the template ships multiple hub variants.
- Publishing `nimbus-docs`-style npm packages.
- Touching the hub-side AwareRide sync skill or real deploy targets.
